  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 225 PM CDT Sat Oct 24 2026\n\nTonight through Sunday:\n\nFollowing a calm, cool, and partly cloudy night tonight \n(relative to this afternoon's warmth), Sunday has a decent \nchance to be one of the warmest days of this current stretch.\nMid and higher level cloud cover may limit temps from really\noverperforming, though currently expecting enough sun for\nwidespread mid 70s highs away from the immediate Illinois shore.\nLocalized upper 70s readings are plausible, especially over\nsouthwestern sections of the CWA (ie. in/near Pontiac). \n\nSunday Night through Saturday:\n\nA backdoor cold front will move across the area Sunday night,\nknocking temps down vs. the weekend for Monday's highs, but \nstill above average for late October. The coolest readings \n(around 60F/low 60s) will be found near Lake Michigan due to \nstrengthening north-northeast winds. Expansive surface high\npressure over the region on Monday night will likely yield the \ncoolest night of the week (still solidly above normal for late \nOctober). \n\nTuesday will warm back to farther above average, followed by \nanother period of well above average temps (highs approaching \n80F in spots?!) centered on midweek. Chances for rain mid to \nlate next week, while not zero, are low/nebulous, and the best \nchance for anything of note looks to be confined to primarily \nwest and north of the local area. If a weakening cold front is \nable to push south across at least the northern half of the area\nThursday-Thursday night, that would result in lower temps than \nin the official forecast (especially near the lake).\n\nThere has been a more consistent signal for a stronger synoptic\nsystem or two over the second half of next weekend into the\nfollowing workweek. First a warm front will lift north Friday-\nFriday night, giving way to what may shape up to be one of the\nwarmest Halloweens in years. For trick or treating interests, \nwhile the official forecast advertises the arrival of low rain \nchances during the day on Saturday, the ensemble consensus \nfavors late Saturday night into Sunday for widespread rainfall.\n\nCastro",
